A basic approach:

```javascript
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const start = Date.now();
  res.on('finish', () => {
    const duration = Date.now() - start;
    console.log(`${req.method} ${req.path} ${res.statusCode} ${duration}ms`);
  });
  next();
});
```

This logs method, path, status code, and duration for every request. Place it before the routes so it wraps all of them.

To include the authenticated user, put the logging after sessionUser and reference `req.user.id`. To capture request body (for auditing writes), log `req.body` before the response finishes, but be careful not to log passwords or sensitive fields.

Alternatively, use the morgan package, which provides structured HTTP request logging with preset formats.

