```
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const start = Date.now();
  const originalJson = res.json;
  res.json = function(data) {
    console.log(`${req.method} ${req.path} ${res.statusCode} ${Date.now() - start}ms`);
    return originalJson.call(this, data);
  };
  next();
});
```

This logs method, path, status code, and elapsed time for each request.

For more detail (request body, response shape), log inside each route handler or use a library. The middleware approach catches all routes in one place but won't see route-specific context.

